From b7aebd38c380aca66c77d2a563cb7132f0ce07aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 13:04:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Herald and page: placement, seed and the extension ceiling on
 screen

The herald's season record and /h/world now state the effective rMax
(the Frontier's r_max_ext once ExtendFrontier raised it), the season's
own r_max, the extension ceiling (0: none), the hard limit 128, the
prize tally's last ring 17 (shown, not changed), the first-home
placement, the heartland rings and the genesis seed.

The page already decodes placement and seed from the Season bytes the
record carries; a test now drives that path from a herald-shaped record
to the join panel's candidates (the program's pinned home_nation
vector). A season with a ceiling tells three more place states apart:
extendable (within the ceiling, not on the map yet), beyond the ceiling,
and beyond ring 128; the ceiling is drawn as a faint second border.
Seasons without a ceiling keep the four states and their words. A march
planned by frontier.wasm crosses from ring 4 into a newly seeded ring 5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C5Nj2bji8di3758qGdC2v1
